      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T04:38:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried that `-EEXIST` here reports the page at `dst_addr` as already mapped when only one of its window siblings is. `move_pages()` stops at that address and returns the bytes moved so far, so userspace that skips a mapped destination on `-EEXIST` would skip a slice that was never moved.\n\nThe other refusals here return `-EBUSY`, as does `p3s_uffd_move_nr_slices()` when a destination sibling isn\u0027t none, and aosp/4368005 uses `-EBUSY` for cross-phase moves. Could this return `-EBUSY` too? Userspace then falls back to UFFDIO_COPY, which returns `-EEXIST` only for the slice that is actually mapped.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c4e1ee3a497d90254b40d032919140b076dc4bfd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
